Citizens turn back lifeless without Rāma --- Households weep with tear-veiled faces --- Markets close and kitchens cook no food --- Mothers take no joy in firstborn or wealth --- Wives reproach husbands and praise LakṣmaṆa --- Envy blest rivers pools forests Rāma will grace --- Long to follow Rāma shade and serve Sītā --- Curse kin-destroying Kaikēyī and refuse her rule --- Foretell Daśaratha death and ruin after him --- Lament falsely exiled Rāma like men facing death
